# ADM-Cube research arm fill: keep the console's running slots occupied.
# Install or refresh with: /home/lzp/miniconda3/envs/quant/bin/python ops/cron/install_tushare_cron.py --block research
#
# The round files below, in order, are the arm queue. Each file's `--fill`
# asks /api/health how many of the console's slots and GPUs are free, skips
# the arms whose experiment directory already exists and creates the next
# pending ones in file order, through the same validation the operator gets
# from `--dry-run`; a local arm the local-model limit holds, or a GPU arm too
# few free cards hold, stays pending and the arms behind it go ahead. The next
# file reads the slots afresh, so it takes what the earlier ones left. Nothing
# pending or nothing free is the steady state and exits 0; a refused creation
# in any file makes the run exit non-zero with its reason in the log, and the
# files after it still fill. The operator tops the queue up by appending arms
# and their reference packs to a file, or a file to ROUNDS; a round whose arms
# have all been created, or whose remaining arms are withdrawn, is marked closed
# and leaves ROUNDS in the same change.

SHELL=/bin/bash
PATH=/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin
CRON_TZ=Asia/Shanghai
REPO_ROOT=/Data2/lzp/ADMCubeQuant
QUANT_PYTHON=/home/lzp/miniconda3/envs/quant/bin/python
# The queue's round files, filled in this order; separated by spaces.
ROUNDS=scripts/experiments/create_round_20261011.py scripts/experiments/create_round_20261012.py

# Every ten minutes, all day: a slot that frees up stays empty for at most that
# long, and research arms end at no particular hour. One run takes seconds per
# file unless it creates, and `flock -n` skips a run while an earlier one is
# still creating, so two fills can never take the same slot.
*/10 * * * * cd $REPO_ROOT && mkdir -p logs/research .runtime/research && flock -n .runtime/research/cron.lock bash -c 'status=0; for round in $ROUNDS; do $QUANT_PYTHON $round 38888 --fill || status=1; done; exit $status' >> logs/research/cron.log 2>&1
